From 7932dbdbea3bb251864697b9f12b9b6413f00eed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mark Ma <coredroid0401@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 19:17:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [Test] Committed recurrent state for one-token prompt tails
 on FULL graphs

Model-free coverage for the state invariant behind #58400: after a step in
which a cached one-token prompt tail (optionally padded with K placeholder
drafts) rides the FULL decode graph, the recurrent state bytes the next step
reads must equal the eager, unpadded execution's, and no placeholder-derived
state may become the committed state.

Drives the real gather_batch_req_state, MambaHybridModelState.prepare_attn at
CUDAGraphMode.FULL and NONE, GDNAttentionMetadataBuilder.build and
MambaHybridModelState.postprocess_state over synthetic conv/SSM pools; the
mixer is a reimplementation of the three state-write contracts, each cited to
its source. Includes a negative control that routes the padded tail through
the prefill write contract and requires the same expectations to fail.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VLD8eK1yhEDSqocmQkR7ty
